{
  "dom_id": "step-q16918",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the general formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence that begins with \n\n$$\n2,\\,11,\\,20,\\,…\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nFrom the first few terms\n\n$$\n2,\\,11,\\,20,\\,…,\n$$\n\nwe see that the first term is $f(1)=2$ and the common difference is \n\n$$\nd=11-2=9.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =2+(n-1)(9) \\\\  & =2+9n-9 \\\\  & =9n-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n        \n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is $f(n)=9n-7.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
